# Prisma migration files must check out as LF on every platform.
#
# Prisma records the sha256 of the raw migration.sql bytes into
# _prisma_migrations.checksum at apply time, while git stores these blobs as LF.
# With core.autocrlf=true (Windows default) and no attribute here, the working
# tree was CRLF, so the recorded checksum disagreed with the bytes the repo
# actually holds — and any machine with different line endings recorded a
# different checksum for the same migration.
#
# Pinning eol=lf makes the checked-out bytes deterministic on every platform,
# which is what the recorded checksums are reconciled against.
prisma/migrations/** text eol=lf
